Report an empty DMI identity where the platform has no DMI source.

init_dmi() knows how to read a machine identity on Linux (udev/sysfs,
falling back to "dmi:*") and FreeBSD (kenv), and returns NULL anywhere
else. init_dt() then looks for a devicetree; with neither,
quirks_init_subsystem() fails and libinput loads no quirks at all -- not
even the generic, identity-independent ones.

Kandelo is neither Linux nor FreeBSD and exposes no SMBIOS/DMI or
devicetree firmware identity (docs/posix-status.md, the
/dev/input/event0 row). Returning the
empty identity -- what libinput's own test suite uses -- keeps that
boundary truthful: DMI-matched sections never match, everything else
applies. Upstream-shaped: it names no platform.

--- a/src/quirks.c
+++ b/src/quirks.c
@@ -458,7 +458,11 @@
 #elif defined(__FreeBSD__)
 	return init_dmi_freebsd();
 #else
-	return NULL;
+	/* No DMI source on this platform. Report the empty identity, as the
+	 * test suite does above, so DMI-matched sections never match and the
+	 * rest of the quirks database still loads. Returning NULL here (with
+	 * no devicetree either) made quirks_init_subsystem() fail outright. */
+	return safe_strdup("dmi:");
 #endif
 }
 
